# %% [markdown]
# # DriftSense — 04: Expected-Cost Forecasting & Baseline Benchmarking
#
# **Runtime Type:** Python 3 (CPU or GPU)  
# **Estimated Runtime:** ~1-3 minutes  
# **RAM Needed:** ~2-4 GB  
# **Disk Needed:** ~1 GB  
# **Expected Outputs:**  
# - Model Checkpoints: `runs/<run_id>/models/{seasonal_naive,moving_average,exponential_smoothing,xgboost}.joblib`  
# - Validation Metrics Report: `runs/<run_id>/val_forecast_metrics.json`  
# - Validation Predictions Matrix: `runs/<run_id>/val_forecast_predictions.csv`  
# - Comparative Forecast Visualization: `runs/<run_id>/forecast_comparison.png`  
# - Cryptographically Verified Manifest: `runs/<run_id>/manifest.json`  
#
# > **CRITICAL EVALUATION & ISOLATION INVARIANTS (G6 & A6.4):**  
# > - **A6.4 Test Partition Quarantine:** The test partition ($D_{\text{test}}$, Days 25–30) is strictly locked and quarantined. Model selection and hyperparameter evaluation occur exclusively on validation ($D_{\text{val}}$, Days 19–24). The run manifest MUST NOT contain test predictions.  
# > - **Scale-Independent Metric Selection:** Cloud billing data contains 99.38% exact zeros. Primary model selection is governed by **WAPE** and **sMAPE** to prevent infinite error penalties on near-zero actuals.  
# > - **Target Log-Transform:** Due to extreme right-tail skewness (kurtosis > 250, skew > 13), XGBoost utilizes `log1p` target stabilization.

# %% [markdown]
# ## 1. Setup & Environment Installation

# %%
import os
import sys
import subprocess
from pathlib import Path

# Pinned repository commit SHA or branch for reproducibility
